d4831b93 IS A GUI FIX LIVING IN A SHARED MODULE, which is the inverted case
worth naming. `kicad_exact_fill._this_interpreter()` replaces bare
`sys.executable` in kicad_python_candidates(), because inside KiCad's embedded
python sys.executable is the pcbnew HOST BINARY -- spawning it opened the
application once per call instead of running the refill script. The fix is in
the shared resolver, so both fronts pick it up and the front that was BROKEN
is the GUI. No wiring needed; the parity direction here is CLI-was-fine,
GUI-was-broken, shared-module-fix.

